1. In a WITH clause, build two lists of station_id: the distinct stations in gsod2019 (reported)
   and the stations in the stations table (listed).
2. FULL JOIN the two lists on station_id. A FULL JOIN keeps unmatched rows from both sides
   and fills the missing side with NULL.
3. Use COUNTIF to count the three cases:
   both sides NOT NULL, listed side NULL, reported side NULL.
